No, it's about the rules for a first gift that do not apply to
subsequent gifts.  The first gift has to be co-aligned so it
will be a chaotic/neutral/lawful one, in your case chaotic.
The first gift has to to be racial so orcs and elves have a
further restriction.  There's also the fact that the chances
of the first gift don't change as other artifacts are created
though the odds do effect subsequent gifts.

This means there are strategies for lawful (dip) and chaotic
(name) to consider before the first gift.  For a human
chaotic, naming Sting and Orcrist before your first gift
trims the list of possibilities down to Stormbringer or
Grimtooth.  For an elven chaotic the list goes down to
only Stormbringer.  This suggests that naming is a very
good strategy.  For lawful, Excalibur is an ascendable
artifact so dipping could render sacri-fests unneeded.


